        "original_id": "41bc6690-26f1-5933-b25d-0104f1900544",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Carl Ben Eielson\n- Places: Eielson Air Force Base, Fairbanks, Moose Creek, Alaska\n- Organizations: United States Air Force\n- Roles: aviator, bush pilot, explorer\n\nFacts:\n- Carl Benjamin \"Ben\" Eielson was born on July 20, 1897, and died on November 9, 1929.\n- Carl Benjamin \"Ben\" Eielson was an American aviator, bush pilot, and explorer.\n- Eielson Air Force Base in Alaska is named in honor of Carl Ben Eielson.\n- Eielson Air Force Base is a United States Air Force base located about 26 miles southeast of Fairbanks, Alaska, and just southeast of Moose Creek, Alaska.\n- Eielson Air Force Base has the codes IATA EIL, ICAO PAEI, and FAA LID EIL.",
